# The name, not the face (docs/REPUTATION.md, "The season record"): a new life is a new face, but
# the season record keeps the name an earlier life made. Once a life per leader. And a lie that was
# caught or found out (nmem:lied): the speaker's next greeting says so, once. Greet lines are
# conditional (say?), so the talk screen opens on a line only when it says something new.

conv haven.leader.name
for leader:haven
when seasoned:haven & !met
greet
once
prio reaction
voice haven

node start
  say? seasoned:haven & !met :: I don't know your face, love, but I know the name. {title:haven}, the houses called you, didn't they? Faces change out here. The soup doesn't. Come and sit by the stove.

conv bastion.leader.name
for leader:bastion
when seasoned:bastion & !met
greet
once
prio reaction
voice bastion

node start
  say? seasoned:bastion & !met :: I don't know the face. I know the name: it's in our file as {title:bastion}, from a life the roster remembers. New face, same file. The sentries will be told.

conv redhand.leader.name
for leader:redhand
when seasoned:redhand & !met
greet
once
prio reaction
voice redhand

node start
  say? seasoned:redhand & !met :: Don't know the face. Know the name, though: {title:redhand}. The book never forgets a name. Faces it forgets all the time, which is lucky for some people.

conv halcyon.leader.name
for leader:halcyon
when seasoned:halcyon & !met
greet
once
prio reaction
voice halcyon

node start
  say? seasoned:halcyon & !met :: Different face. Same name in the record: {title:halcyon}, from an earlier life. We'll treat you as a repeat measurement and see whether the result holds.

conv haven.leader.lied
for leader:haven
when nmem:lied
greet
once
prio quest
voice haven

node start
  say? nmem:lied :: You told me something that wasn't true, and I found out. I'm not angry. I'm just counting differently now, and so will the house.

conv bastion.leader.lied
for leader:bastion
when nmem:lied
greet
once
prio quest
voice bastion

node start
  say? nmem:lied :: What you told me last time didn't check out. It's in your file now, next to everything else, and the sentries read the file.

conv redhand.leader.lied
for leader:redhand
when nmem:lied
greet
once
prio quest
voice redhand

node start
  say? nmem:lied :: You lied to me. To me! In my own camp. I'd be impressed if I wasn't busy writing it in the book.

conv halcyon.leader.lied
for leader:halcyon
when nmem:lied
greet
once
prio quest
voice halcyon

node start
  say? nmem:lied :: Your account didn't replicate. The discrepancy is in the record now, with your initials beside it.

conv wanderer.deserter.picture
for wanderer:deserter
when tier:bastion!=stranger
topic "What does Bastion make of me?"
prio flavour
daily
voice plain

node start
  say? rep:bastion=necessary_evil :: Bastion's got you down as a Necessary Evil. That means they'll use you till you're used up, and log every use. Ask me how I know.
  say? rep:bastion=useful_trouble :: Useful Trouble, they call you. They'll smile at you at the wire and write it down after. Both, every time.
  say? hunted:bastion :: You're Hunted by them. Welcome to the club. There's no club. There's a ditch, a cold camp and a lot of looking over your shoulder.
  say? tier:bastion>=trusted :: They trust you. I was trusted once, at a post past the hills. It's a lovely feeling, right up until they read you an order.
  say They've got you on a board somewhere, in grease pencil, with a line about where you were last seen. Grease pencil rubs off. Remember that.
  > @why Why did you leave them? -> why
  > @back Let me ask something else. -> hub

node why
  say Same reason anyone leaves. A sergeant read out an order, and for once I heard it properly. I won't say what it was. You'd only go and look.
  say Bastion writes people like me up as killed in action. It's kinder than the other word, and it means somebody is still sent to look.
  > @back1 I won't ask again. -> hub

conv table.road.exile
for table:road
when exiled & !table:crossed
greet
once
voice table

node start
  say? exiled & !table:crossed :: Put out, were you? The houses do that, love. Counting, always counting. We don't count. We just make room. Is anyone expecting you back tonight?
